    "problem_statement": "Query initialization broken with strict mode and query strings\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen initializing a Query object with a query string, the parsing is broken. The query string gets incorrectly processed, causing various issues with parameter parsing and access.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport furl\n\n# Basic query string parsing fails\nq = furl.Query('a=1&b=2')\nprint(q.params)  # Expected: {'a': '1', 'b': '2'}, but gets different result\n\n# Unicode handling broken\nq = furl.Query('ロリポップ=testä')\nprint(q.params['ロリポップ'])  # Should work but raises KeyError\n\n# Empty query handling issues\nq = furl.Query('slrp')\nprint(str(q))  # Expected: 'slrp', but gets different output\n```\n\nThe issue affects basic query string initialization and parameter access. Query strings that should parse correctly are not being handled properly, breaking fundamental functionality of the Query class."
